{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Matsumoto","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhatOrder"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.bruhatLe_trans_An","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.bruhatLe_trans_An","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L251-L254","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.subword_property_An","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.subword_property_An","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L245-L249","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.bruhatLe_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.bruhatLe_trans","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L232-L241","doc":"**Transitivity** — the second of `CoxeterBruhat`'s four, and a two-line consequence of the\nsubword property.\n\nThe obstruction `CoxeterBruhatOrder` recorded was that `u ≤ v` names *some* reduced word for `v`\nwhile `v ≤ w` produces *another* one. The subword property removes the distinction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.bruhatLe_iff_forall_reduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.bruhatLe_iff_forall_reduced","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L218-L228","doc":"The existential definition of `BruhatLe` is equivalent to the universal one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.subword_property","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.subword_property","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L208-L216","doc":"**The subword property.** If `u ≤ w` then **every** reduced word for `w` has a subword\nmultiplying to `u` — not merely the one the definition happens to name. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.hasSubwordFor_of_braidEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.hasSubwordFor_of_braidEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L198-L204","doc":"Hence braid-**equivalence** preserves it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.hasSubwordFor_of_braidMove","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.hasSubwordFor_of_braidMove","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L180-L196","doc":"**A braid move preserves the property.** Outside the rewritten block nothing moves; inside it,\n`exists_subword_altWord_swap` supplies the replacement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.HasSubwordFor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.HasSubwordFor","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L177-L178","doc":"\"`ω` has a subword multiplying to `u`\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.exists_subword_altWord_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.exists_subword_altWord_swap","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L126-L173","doc":"**The one piece of real content.** A subword of `altWord i j (M i j)` has a same-product\nsubword of `altWord j i (M j i)`.\n\nThe subword's product `v` lies in the rank-two parabolic and has length at most `M i j`; by\n`CoxeterRankTwo` it has an **alternating** reduced word, of one spelling or the other. The prefix\nand tail facts cover every case but `ℓ(v) = M i j` in the wrong spelling, and there the braid\nrelation says the whole target word already has product `v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.wordProd_altWord_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.wordProd_altWord_braid","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L112-L122","doc":"**The braid relation.** The two alternating words of length `M i j` have the same product.\nMathlib states it for `alternatingWord`; the bridge carries it to `altWord`, in both parities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.altWord_swap_sublist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.altWord_swap_sublist","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L97-L103","doc":"**Other spelling: a tail.** `altWord j i k` sits inside `altWord i j n` for `k < n` — drop the\nleading letter and apply the prefix fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.altWord_sublist_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.altWord_sublist_self","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L85-L95","doc":"**Same spelling: a prefix.** `altWord i j k` is a prefix of `altWord i j n` for `k ≤ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.mem_altWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword.mem_altWord","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatSubword.lean#L73-L83","doc":"Every letter of an alternating word is one of its two indices. ","signatureChunk":0}]}